---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: MCP server
description: Generate color ramps, spacing and type scales, and light and dark themes, and check contrast, from any MCP client.
---

{% set pkg = packages.mcp %}
{% include "partials/package-links.njk" %}

<p>
  The Quieto MCP server gives an AI assistant the tools of
  <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@quieto/tokens" rel="noopener">Quieto Tokens</a>,
  so it can build an accessible token system, or check one, while it works on
  your code. It is hosted, so there is nothing to install: point your client at
  <code>{{ ai.mcp.url }}</code>.
</p>

<h2 id="connect">Connect your client</h2>

<qds-tabs label="MCP clients" class="client-tabs">
  <qds-tab slot="tab">Claude Code</qds-tab>
  <qds-tab slot="tab">Cursor</qds-tab>
  <qds-tab slot="tab">VS Code</qds-tab>
  <qds-tab slot="tab">Claude Desktop</qds-tab>
  <qds-tab slot="tab">Other clients</qds-tab>

  <qds-tab-panel>
    <p>Run, in your project:</p>
    <pre><code>claude mcp add quieto --transport http {{ ai.mcp.url }}</code></pre>
  </qds-tab-panel>

  <qds-tab-panel>
    <p>
      Add the server to <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> for one project, or to
      <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code> for all of them:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "quieto": {
      "url": "{{ ai.mcp.url }}"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
  </qds-tab-panel>

  <qds-tab-panel>
    <p>
      Add the server to <code>.vscode/mcp.json</code>. VS Code's key is
      <code>servers</code>, not <code>mcpServers</code>:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{
  "servers": {
    "quieto": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "{{ ai.mcp.url }}"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
  </qds-tab-panel>

  <qds-tab-panel>
    <p>
      In <strong>Settings → Connectors</strong>, choose <strong>Add custom
      connector</strong>, name it Quieto, and enter <code>{{ ai.mcp.url }}</code>.
    </p>
  </qds-tab-panel>

  <qds-tab-panel>
    <p>
      Any client that speaks Streamable HTTP can connect to
      <code>{{ ai.mcp.url }}</code>. Older clients that only speak SSE can use
      <code>{{ ai.mcp.sseUrl }}</code>.
    </p>
  </qds-tab-panel>
</qds-tabs>

<h2 id="tools">Tools</h2>

<div class="table-scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for tool in ai.mcp.tools %}
        <tr><td><code>{{ tool.name }}</code></td><td>{{ tool.what }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 id="prompts">Try it</h2>

<p>Once connected, ask for what you want; the assistant picks the tools:</p>

<ul>
  {% for prompt in ai.mcp.prompts %}<li>{{ prompt }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>

<p>
  The server builds and checks tokens. It does not document the QDS components
  yet; for those, use these pages.
</p>
